  "title": "Erdős Problem #1133",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $C>0$. There exists $\\epsilon>0$ such that if $n$ is sufficiently large the following holds.\nFor any $x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\in [-1,1]$ there exist $y_1,\\ldots,y_n\\in [-1,1]$ such that, if $P$ is a polynomial of degree $m<(1+\\epsilon)n$ with $P(x_i)=y_i$ for at least $(1-\\epsilon)n$ many $1\\leq i\\leq n$, then $ \\max_{x\\in [-1,1]}\\lvert P(x)\\rvert >C. $ ",
